    "pl_faq": {
      "type": "pl-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I know which size to get?",
            "answer": "<p>Measure your dog nose to base of tail while they are lying stretched out, then add 15–20cm. If they are between two sizes, size up, because dogs that sprawl need the length more than you would think. Our <a href=\"/pages/size-guide\">size guide</a> has the breed-by-breed detail, and if you get it wrong the 100-night trial covers it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much is delivery, and how quickly does it arrive?",
            "answer": "<p>UK delivery is free on orders over £40 and £4.99 below that, normally arriving in 3–5 working days. Express is £6.99 at checkout and normally arrives in 2–3. Orders are dispatched within 1–2 working days and you get tracking as soon as it leaves us.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I pay in instalments?",
            "answer": "<p>If Klarna is available on your order you will see it at checkout, where you can split the cost into three interest-free payments. The instalment figure shown on this page is the real one for the size you have selected.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does 50kg/m³ actually mean?",
            "answer": "<p>It is the density of the foam: how much material is packed into every cubic metre. Density is not the same as firmness: a low-density foam can feel firm on day one and still collapse by month six. High-density foam keeps its structure under repeated weight, which is why a 50kg/m³ core is still supporting hips and elbows years later, and why we can put a 5-year guarantee on it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it help a dog with arthritis or hip problems?",
            "answer": "<p>Our supportive beds distribute weight so pressure is not concentrated on hips, elbows and shoulders, which is what makes lying down and getting up harder for dogs with joint wear. A bed is not a treatment and will not replace veterinary care, so please keep talking to your vet. What it can change is the surface they spend fourteen hours a day on.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I actually wash it?",
            "answer": "<p>On most of our beds, yes, properly, not just spot-clean. The cover zips off and goes in the machine at 30°C, and on waterproof-lined beds the foam core is protected so wet coats and accidents never reach it. Outdoor kennels and rattan pieces hose down instead. The care line in the specification tells you which applies here.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if my dog just won't use it?",
            "answer": "<p>Then it goes back and you are not out of pocket. Let your dog sleep on it for up to 100 nights. If it is not the bed for them, contact us inside that window and we arrange the return and refund every penny. Full terms are in our <a href=\"/policies/refund-policy\">returns policy</a>.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
